1. Purpose

This repository implements DUME (Data Universal Manifold Encoder) — a modular, production-grade latent manifold compression system for high-dimensional streaming data.

The system is designed for:

Real-time streaming latent encoding
Manifold-based compression and reconstruction
Distributed-safe state evolution
Low-latency inference under memory constraints
Pluggable cryptographic and compression layers

2. 🧱 Repository Structure (STRICT)

This repo MUST follow Swift Package Manager layout:

DUME/
├── Package.swift
├── Sources/
│   ├── DUMECore/
│   ├── DUMECompression/
│   ├── DUMEMetrics/
│   ├── DUMEStorage/
│   ├── DUMEEncryption/
│   ├── DUMEEngine/
│   └── DUMEFoundation/
├── Tests/
│   ├── DUMECoreTests/
│   ├── DUMECompressionTests/
│   ├── DUMEEngineTests/
│   └── DUMEIntegrationTests/
├── Examples/
│   └── BasicUsage.swift
├── Benchmarks/
│   └── LatencyBench.swift
├── Scripts/
│   └── healthcheck.swift
└── README.md

3. Swift Package Requirements
Package.swift MUST define:
Modular targets (no monolithic target allowed)
Separate test targets per module
iOS + macOS compatibility

Required minimum:

Swift Tools: 5.9+
Platforms:
iOS 16+
macOS 13+

4. Core Architecture Rules
4.1 Dependency Direction Rule (STRICT)

Allowed dependency flow:

DUMECore
   ↓
DUMECompression
   ↓
DUMEEngine
   ↓
Application Layer

Forbidden:
Storage depending on Engine
Compression depending on Engine
Crypto depending on Core runtime state

4.2 Stateless Core Requirement

All core modules MUST:

Avoid global state
Avoid static mutation
Be deterministic given input
4.3 Pluggable Interfaces Required

The system MUST expose protocols for:

DUMEMetric
DUMECompressionPolicy
DUMEStorageEngine
DUMEEncryption

All implementations MUST be swappable at runtime via factory injection.

5. Security Requirements
AES-GCM only allowed encryption baseline
No plaintext persistence in storage layer
Encryption must be optional via config flag
No crypto assumptions in core engine

6. Performance Requirements
The system MUST:

Avoid O(n²) operations in ingestion path (except nearest neighbor fallback mode)
Use SIMD where available (Accelerate framework required)
Support streaming ingestion without blocking
Keep reconstruction O(n) or better
7. Testing Requirements (CI GATE)

All PRs MUST pass:
7.1 Unit Tests
Compression correctness
Reconstruction integrity
Metric consistency
7.2 Integration Tests
ingest → compress → store → reconstruct cycle
encryption round-trip validation
7.3 Determinism Test

Same input MUST produce same latent state:
hash(input) → hash(output) must match across runs

8. Health Check Contract (MANDATORY)

Repo MUST include: Which validates:

Engine builds successfully
Ingest pipeline runs
Reconstruction does not fail
No runtime crashes under sample load

Exit codes:

0 = healthy
1 = broken build or logic failure

9. Benchmark Requirements

Benchmark suite MUST measure:

Ingest latency per vector
Reconstruction latency
Compression ratio
Memory footprint per anchor
SIMD acceleration gain

Benchmarks MUST be reproducible and deterministic.

10. Example Usage (MUST EXIST)

Repo MUST include:
let engine = DUMEBootstrap.build()

engine.ingest(
    id: "sample",
    vector: [0.1, 0.2, 0.3],
    ctx: CompressionContext(entropy: 0.2, drift: 0.1)
)

let result = engine.retrieve(id: "sample")
11. CI/CD REQUIREMENTS (GitHub Actions)

Pipeline MUST include:

swift build
swift test
healthcheck execution
benchmark run (non-blocking allowed but reported)

Fail conditions:

test failure
build failure
determinism mismatch

12. Versioning Policy

Semantic versioning required:MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH
Rules:

MAJOR → architecture break
MINOR → feature addition (new module/plugin)
PATCH → performance fix / bug fix

13. Forbidden Practices

The following are NOT allowed:

Global mutable state
Hidden singleton engines
Hard-coded cryptographic keys
Mixed abstraction layers in same file
Direct memory reinterpretation without codec layer
Circular module dependencies

14. Design Philosophy

DUME is NOT:

a database
a neural network
a compression utility

DUME IS:

A deterministic manifold state machine for streaming latent evolution under bounded memory and compute constraints.

15.  Repository Acceptance Criteria

A PR can only be merged if:

 Builds successfully via SwiftPM
 All tests pass
 Healthcheck returns 0
 No dependency violations
 No unsafe memory operations
 Deterministic output verified
