 Purpose

This repository implements a production-grade hybrid compression + variational memory engine that bridges:

Lightweight deterministic ingestion (production-safe mode)
Optional variational manifold evolution (high-fidelity mode)
Speculative reconstruction under controlled confidence
Burst-safe degradation handling
Persistent, recoverable vector memory system

The system is designed for:

High-throughput vector ingestion
Drift-tolerant memory retrieval
Optional graph evolution (manifold layer)
Safe fallback under entropy spikes
Deterministic production behavior by default

Core Architecture Requirements
1. Engine Modes (Mandatory)

The system MUST support 3 runtime phases:

coldStart → initialization + no speculation
warming → partial optimization enabled
active → full manifold + speculation enabled

Transitions must be deterministic and based on ingestion count or explicit override.

2. Modular Feature Flags (Mark 6 Add-on Requirement)

The “Mark 6 add-on follow-up” is implemented as runtime toggles, not compile-time forks.

Required feature flags:
enableEvolution → enables manifold graph updates
enableSpeculation → enables predictive reconstruction
enableBurstProtection → enables entropy gating
enablePersistence → enables disk-backed anchors
enableCrypto → enables encryption layer

Each subsystem MUST degrade gracefully when disabled.

3. Manifold Layer (Optional Graph Engine)
If enabled:
Nodes represent compressed anchors
k-NN edges (k ≤ 3 default)
Utility-based decay pruning required
No global reindexing allowed (O(1) local updates preferred)

Acceptance: Graph must remain consistent after insert/delete cycles
No memory leaks from orphaned neighbor references

4. Speculative Engine
If enabled:
Must predict vector evolution using local velocity approximation
Must include confidence score [0.0–1.0]
Must be ignored automatically when:
burst mode is active
confidence < threshold

Acceptance: No speculative overwrite allowed without validation gate
Deterministic fallback to raw vector required

5. Burst Protection System
Required behavior:
Monitor entropy drift delta
Enter burst mode when threshold exceeded
In burst mode:
Disable compression
Disable speculation
Preserve full fidelity ingestion

Acceptance:
Zero data loss during burst state transitions
Burst exit must not corrupt prior anchors

6. Persistence Layer
Must support:
Async anchor storage
Full checkpoint/restore cycle
JSON or binary encoding (implementation choice)

Acceptance:
Restart restores identical vector state
No partial corruption allowed on crash simulation

7. Compression System
Rules:
Sparse encoding using thresholding
Adaptive threshold based on:
entropy
drift
burst state

Acceptance:
Must guarantee index-value alignment integrity
Must not exceed O(n) compression complexity per vector

8. Thread Safety
Required:
Graph mutations must be lock-protected or actor-isolated
Storage must be actor-safe
No shared mutable state outside controlled boundaries

